description:
docs/11-video.md (Compiler wiring section, added in commit 723c640/task 1218) states: 'When the dataURI demuxes to real frames, NumFrames/Width/Height/CodecID come from the demuxed stream.' This is factually wrong for Width/Height.

In packages/swf/src/compiler/media.ts runMediaPass, the emitted DefineVideoStream (tag 60) Width/Height come UNCONDITIONALLY from videoItem.width / videoItem.height (the library model values), lines ~97-98:
  const width = Math.max(0, Math.round(videoItem.width));
  const height = Math.max(0, Math.round(videoItem.height));
Only NumFrames (payloads.length) and CodecID (flvCodecToSwfCodec(flv.codecId)) are derived from the demux. The demuxFlv() return value's width/height fields — produced by the parseFlvMetaDims() (onMetaData AMF0) and parseH263Dims() (Sorenson H.263 bitstream) extractors in video.ts — are NEVER read by any compiler code (grep: flv.width / flv.height have zero consumers outside video.ts itself). So the entire dimension-extraction subsystem documented under the doc's 'FLV demux' heading is effectively dead code with respect to the emitted SWF.

EVIDENCE: compiled a doc with a real 3-frame H.263 FLV data URI where videoItem.width=128/height=96 but the demuxed FLV resolves to the 320x240 fallback. swf-dump (Ruffle's swf crate) of the output:
  DefineVideoStream { id:1, num_frames:3, width:128, height:96, codec:H263 }
=> width/height = 128/96 (model), NOT 320/240 (demux). The existing unit test 'compiles a real FLV data URI into matching tag-60/tag-61 payloads' (videostream.test.ts:738) even sets videoItem.width/height to match the assertion, masking the divergence.

NOTE: the emit is otherwise structurally valid and Ruffle-parseable (tags 60/61 byte layout matches ruffle/swf/src/read.rs read_define_video_stream/read_video_frame; PlaceObject2 references the video char). Only the doc is wrong.

FIX OPTIONS (pick one): (a) correct the doc to say Width/Height come from the VideoItem model, and note the demuxed dims are advisory/currently unused; OR (b) make runMediaPass prefer flv.width/flv.height when the demux yields real dimensions (then the doc becomes true and the extraction code becomes live). Do NOT touch ease/tween files. Coordinate so videoFitTransform still fits native->display correctly if (b) is chosen.
